> Mike Price:
> 
> > >   If a skilled "20-questions" player can get the answer
> > >   most of the time, then the size of the societally-common
> > >   "object" knowledge is about 2^20 or one million "objects".
> > > 
> > Definitely flawed.  The unskilled/stupider players need more questions
> > to get to the answer.  By the above logic they 'know' more. ?????
